# bl show for bugs/ideas should include File stats and body preview like tasks

## Context

Task `show` already prints `File stats: N bytes, M lines` and a body preview (12 lines default, with `--long` / `--all`). Bug and idea `show` only print a thin summary (id/title/status/estimate/file path) and omit stats and body. Residual gap after closing B015 (task-path work).

## Steps to Reproduce

1. `bl show P1.M1.E1.T001` — note File stats + Preview
2. `bl show B021` (or any bug/idea) — note missing stats and body

## Expected Behavior

For bugs and ideas, `bl show` should match task-show ergonomics:

- `File stats: <bytes> bytes, <lines> lines`
- Body/preview of the `.todo` file (default truncated, full with `--long` / `--all`)
- Parity across Go, Python, and TypeScript clients
- Tests covering bug and idea show paths

## Actual Behavior

`renderBugOrIdeaDetail` (Go) and Python aux show path print metadata + file path only; no stats, no preview.
